WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.167 --> 00:00:01.210
Boom!

00:00:02.878 --> 00:00:04.421
Holy shit.
So screw it.

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:05.464
Holy shit!

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.592
Bingo.

00:00:12.471 --> 00:00:16.475
Hey, uh, Henderson's
not a… a curse, is he?

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:18.393
Curse? No. No, no, no.
He's fine.

00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:19.436
Mental?

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.146
Absolutely.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.233
You guys stay here with Max.
Keep an eye out for trouble.

00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:25.317
You keep an eye out!

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.570
-It's my goddamn theory.
-You heard Nance.

00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:30.197
-Who put her in charge?
-I did.

00:00:30.948 --> 00:00:32.282
Could you maybe, uh…

00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:35.202
clarify what sort of clues

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.037
we're supposed
to be looking for here?

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.667
"The world is full
of obvious things

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.087
which nobody by any chance
ever observes."

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:49.258
Sherlock Holmes.

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.718
You guys realise, if there's
a gate down there,

00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:53.637
it's technically
a water gate.

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:57.140
Watergate!

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.561
It's north.

00:01:00.644 --> 00:01:02.062
I'm positive,
I checked the map.

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:03.188
You do realise
that Skull Rock

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:04.565
it's like a super popular
make-out spot?

00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:05.524
Yeah, so?

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:06.650
Yeah, well,
it wasn't popular

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.986
until I made it popular,
all right?

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.028
I practically invented it.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:11.196
We're heading
 to the wrong direction.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.990
Maybe you infiltrated
his mind.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.616
He invaded your mind, right?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:15.993
Is it that big of a leap
to suggest

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.703
you somehow wound up in his?

00:01:18.287 --> 00:01:19.955
Like Freddy Krueger's
boiler room.

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:21.373
Freddy Krueger?

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:23.500
He's this
super burned-up dude

00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:24.960
with razors for fingers

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:26.378
and he kills you
in your dreams.

00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:28.130
Dustin, seriously?

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.673
Sorry.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.675
It's a movie. It's not real.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.218
Boom!

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:38.140
Bada bada boom.

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:40.517
I was right.

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:43.020
Skull Rock was north.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.313
Seriously? You're serious?

00:01:45.314 --> 00:01:46.982
This is Skull Rock! OK?

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:49.902
You're totally, absolutely
100 per cent wrong.

00:01:49.985 --> 00:01:51.445
-Right now!
-Yes.

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:53.780
And no.

00:01:53.864 --> 00:01:54.865
Oh, my God.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.533
That thing's got
batteries in it, right?

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:01.163
I'm not even answering
that question.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:02.873
This compass
worked correctly

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.416
when we left the Wheelers'.

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:06.627
It was correct when we got
in the car on Curly, but it

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.670
started to slip
the further east we went.

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:11.256
Now, it's way off.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.842
When I was leading us here,
I wasn't wrong.

00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:15.302
The compass was.

00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:16.720
So you're using
faulty equipment.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.055
Dude, you're still wrong.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.932
Except it isn't faulty.

00:02:20.015 --> 00:02:21.892
You guys understand
any of this?

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.477
-No.
-Pretty straightforward.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:24.895
Oh, straightforward. Really?

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.104
Well, what's confusing
to you?

00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:29.107
Why is this wizard
obsessed with clocks?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.737
Maybe he's like a clockmaker
or something?

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.823
I think you cracked
the case, Steve.

00:02:37.366 --> 00:02:39.284
The chances of success
are 20 to 1.

00:02:39.368 --> 00:02:42.287
Never tell me the odds.

00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:44.540
Remember when I said they
wouldn't be stupid enough

00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:45.916
to go through Watergate?

00:02:47.376 --> 00:02:48.460
Yeah.

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:52.047
I overestimated them.

00:02:54.925 --> 00:02:56.093
Where did everyone
get those?

00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:00.931
Do you need
to be told everything?

00:03:02.474 --> 00:03:03.600
You're not a child.

00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:06.103
-The freak, right?
-Exactly.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:08.063
-Shit.
-So before that happens,

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:09.439
we need to find Vecna,

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:10.774
kill him and prove
your innocence.

00:03:10.858 --> 00:03:12.734
That's all, Dustin?
That's all?

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:14.486
Yeah, no,
that's pretty much it.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.821
So screw it.

00:03:16.655 --> 00:03:17.698
Screw what?

00:03:18.282 --> 00:03:19.741
Screw high school!

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:21.785
What? What?

00:03:22.661 --> 00:03:23.787
Dustin? Where are you going?

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.080
Just trust me!

00:03:25.664 --> 00:03:26.999
Come on! Just talk to me!

00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:28.834
Tell me things!

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.127
Wear a helmet!

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.796
Vecna is his
five-star general,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.256
a five-star general

00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:36.300
with the power
to open gates.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.051
Holy shit!

00:03:38.135 --> 00:03:39.511
-Holy shit!
-Holy shit!

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.096
Here goes nothing.

00:03:46.435 --> 00:03:47.728
There we go.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.773
And if my theory is correct…

00:03:54.902 --> 00:03:57.321
-Abracadabra.
-Holy shit.

00:03:57.404 --> 00:03:58.947
Anybody understand
what he's talking about?

00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:00.365
-No.
-No idea.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.454
OK, seriously?

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:08.332
How many times do I have
to be right on the money

00:04:08.415 --> 00:04:10.125
before you guys
just trust me?

00:04:10.209 --> 00:04:12.127
Jesus Christ, this kid's
gotta get his ego in check.

00:04:12.211 --> 00:04:14.087
-It's his tone, right?
-Screw it.

00:04:15.881 --> 00:04:17.424
Let's kill
the son of a bitch.

